# G0.3 review R2-01: sharing an item provider through the system share sheet on the simulator (observation)
# Environment: simulator, iPhone 17, iOS 26.5 (23F77), device Sylvia-M0-minors-g03-intake; host macOS 26.6.2 (25G83).
# Test: IntakeHarnessUITests/ShareSheetUITests/testCancelWhileProviderIsStillDelivering. The harness shares an
# NSItemProvider whose EPUB file representation reports progress every 100 ms for 90 s before it delivers; the test
# opens Sylvia Intake Spike from the share sheet and taps Cancel while nothing has been delivered yet.
# Command (each run): xcodebuild test-without-building -project G03Intake.xcodeproj -scheme IntakeHarness
#   -destination id=<this simulator> -derivedDataPath .build/DerivedData -only-testing:<the test>
# Times are UTC; the simulator log prints local time (UTC+13), shown in brackets.

## 1. Share sheet built from UIActivityItemsConfiguration(itemProviders: [provider]) (commit 3449a8b's harness)
Run 2026-10-12T22:21:44Z-22:22:55Z: FAILED at ShareSheetUITests.swift:128, the extension's "share.copying" text did not
appear within 60 s. XCTest's trace:
    t =     4.69s Tap "harness.shareSlow" Button
    t =     6.51s Tap "shareCell" Cell            (the cell labelled "Sylvia Intake Spike")
    t =     6.93s Waiting 60.0s for "share.copying" StaticText to exist
Simulator log over the same window (22:21:45Z-22:23:00Z [11:21:45-11:23:00]):
    sharingd: "Created share activity proxy ... activity:<UISocialActivity ...> activityType:com.jevidon.sylvia.spike.intake.share"
              at 22:21:51.572Z [11:21:51.572], so the sheet listed the extension;
    no line from an IntakeShare process (log predicate: process == "IntakeShare"): the extension never launched;
    no "G03-SLOWPROVIDER" line from the harness: the share sheet never asked the provider for its file.
The tap selected nothing; the sheet stayed up until the test ended.

## 2. The provider passed as an activity item: UIActivityViewController(activityItems: [provider], applicationActivities: nil)
Run 2026-10-12T23:07:47Z-23:08:11Z (after rebuilding with this change to the share sheet; the same build also changed
the document picker's evidence line, which this test does not touch): passed.
    G03-EVIDENCE cancel before delivery: extension showed 'Zero KB copied' when Cancel was tapped; 'Not received. Nothing
    was saved to Sylvia.' / 'The copy was cancelled.' 1.5 s after the tap (provider due to deliver at 90 s)
    G03-EVIDENCE cancel before delivery: harness-side provider loads: load 1: started; app summary jobs=5 staged=3 review=2 share=1
    simulator log: 23:07:57.829Z [12:07:57.829] IntakeHarness "G03-SLOWPROVIDER load 1: started"
The clean CI run (ci-clean-run.log, sim-app-tests.log) passed the same way: "load 1: started" at 23:36:43.077Z
[12:36:43.077].

## 3. Whether the extension's Cancel reached the sharing app's provider
In both passing runs the harness's provider logged only "load 1: started": no "asked to stop" (it checks its Progress
for cancellation every 100 ms) and no "delivered" before the test ended and terminated the harness, about 15 s after
the Cancel. Across the process boundary, cancelling the extension's load did not cancel the sharing app's own
Progress within that time on the simulator. The extension is free at once either way (it stops waiting and claims
nothing); the sharing app may go on producing a file nobody waits for. Device checklist steps 9 and 18 record what
Mail and iCloud do.
